      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks dangerous to me, not everything in Chromium is compiled with c++17 (I think parts of the code have transitioned to c++20). This also requires us to keep updating this code whenever the c++ version changes.\n\nUnfortunately, cpp_std / c_std isn\u0027t available in the target.arch properties, so I see the following ways forward:\n- Append \n```\n`android:\"arch_variant\"`\n```\nto C_std and Cpp_std [here](https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/build/soong/cc/compiler.go;l\u003d114) and see what Colin thinks. (Though, it is a little weird for the same library to be built with different cpp versions depending on the target architecture). Of course, this would also break in tm-mainline-prod, but he might be willing to merge this there too.\n- Figure out a way to ignore the cpp version flag of the test target. The best way to do this would probably involve adding cpp_std and c_std properties to GnParser.Target and do the flag parsing inside parse_gn_desc (and assert that once the version is set, it must always match for the other architectures). You would have to add a new parameter indicating if the target your parsing is a test target or not.\n\nDo you have any better ideas?\nMaybe you know why the c++ version (host??) differs?",
